course: dictionary
lesson: 3817
title: Forgetful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Forgetful» is an adjective. It describes someone who often forgets things, like names, homework or where they put something. The word comes from «forget» with «-ful» on the end, which means full of, so a forgetful person is full of forgetting.
explain: The sentences give you clues. «If a grandparent becomes forgetful because of an illness like dementia, they still love you and need patience.» Here forgetful is linked to illness, and the sentence tells you how to treat someone who is forgetful: with patience.
explain: «When an older relative becomes very forgetful because of an illness, the repeating is the illness, not the person being difficult.» Forgetful people often repeat themselves, because they have forgotten they already said it. Try the swap: "a forgetful gardener" means a gardener who often forgets things, and that fits the squirrel sentence.
fact: «Forgetful» means often forgetting things, like names, homework or where you put something.
fact: Forms: forgetful, more forgetful, most forgetful. The noun is «forgetfulness».
fact: Being tired or ill can make people forgetful.
fact: In «Squirrels», the squirrel forgets where it buried some nuts, and «the ones it forgets grow into new trees».
fact: Forgetful people still need kindness, patience and reminders, such as lists and calendars.
exercise: «If a grandparent becomes forgetful because of an illness, they still love you and need patience.» What does forgetful mean here? | *Often forgetting things | Very clever at maths | Always singing loudly | Afraid of the dark
exercise: «The repeating is the illness, not the person being difficult.» Why does the writer say this? | Because the relative is being rude on purpose | Because the relative likes telling jokes twice | Because the relative is bored | *Because forgetting can come from an illness
exercise: What is the noun form of forgetful? | forgets | forgetter | forgetfully | *forgetfulness
test: Which describes a forgetful person? | Winning the spelling test with full marks | Losing her keys and missing her bus again | *Forgetting her lunch box every morning | Singing loudly in the bath
test: In «a forgetful gardener», what does forgetful suggest? | *A gardener who often forgets where things are | A gardener who grows only flowers | A gardener who never plants trees | A gardener who is very strong
exam: Jayden says, «Don't be cross, Grandad is just forgetful, not rude.» What does Jayden mean? | Grandad never forgets anything | Grandad is being rude on purpose | *Grandad often forgets things, so be patient | Grandad is a very fast runner
